From c0a3f5eab0a134fea912cff8ea9a72a28b063c59 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: djvalic <djvalic@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 13:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 32/32] ad5x: Extended memory mode, standard by default

Every AD5X now starts in the same standard memory mode: Kiln's kernels get
the low window alone, without the X2600H's second bank
(mem=256M@0x30000000). On a board with 512 MiB the owner can switch
extended memory on (/data/ad5x/kernel/extended-memory, written by Kiln
OS's ad5x-memory); the bank then stays on the command line.

x2600_args_memory() takes the bank off unless the start is extended on
512 MiB, and appends ad5x.ram=256|512 and ad5x.memmode=standard|extended
for Linux userspace, so that it knows the board's RAM whatever the mode.
U-Boot proper reads the board's RAM once and applies it to every kernel
it starts: the recovery OS is always standard. The SPL's own start of
Kiln's 6.6 from a slot (U-Boot proper missing or failed) is always
standard too, as it can't read the owner's choice and is a fallback;
x2600_args_spl() holds that decision. Flashforge's 5.10 in a slot keeps
the stock SPL's line.

The boot rules decide the mode: extended only for a plain start of the
main OS on Kiln's 6.6 or 7.3 (the starts that get cmdline-extra) that the
owner switched on, on 512 MiB, with no failure recorded on /data
(kernel/extended-memory-failed), not on the first start after an install,
not on a fallback, and only when no start is unconfirmed. The state
sector records "mem ext|std" for each start. An extended start that
doesn't finish is one of the existing tries; the next start is standard
and the records get "failed-mem <reason>" for the main OS to copy to
/data. U-Boot drops that record once a later start has been confirmed:
the copy on /data counts from then on, so the owner switches the mode on
again by removing it. Every failing sequence still ends in the recovery
OS within three unconfirmed starts.

A state or records sector from an older build (no "mem", no
"failed-mem") reads as standard and no record; an older build ignores
both keys.
