+ * - Extended memory (Kiln OS: the X2600H's second bank for the kernel):
+ *   only for a start of the main OS on Kiln's own kernel that the owner
+ *   switched on (/data/ad5x/kernel/extended-memory) on a 512 MiB board,
+ *   not after a failure (kernel/extended-memory-failed), not on the first
+ *   start after an install, not on a fallback, and only when no start is
+ *   unconfirmed (state empty). The state says "mem ext" for such a start;
+ *   one that doesn't finish is one of the tries above, and the next start
+ *   is standard, with "failed-mem" in the records for the main OS to copy
+ *   to /data. That record goes once a later start has been confirmed
